---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/+$/, '');
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How MMAI Media LLC collects, uses, and protects your information, including your GDPR and CCPA rights and how to unsubscribe from our newsletter."
  updated="October 27, 2026"
>
  <p>
    MMAI Media LLC ("<strong>MMAI Media</strong>," "<strong>we</strong>," "<strong>us</strong>," or "<strong>our</strong>"),
    a limited liability company based in San Francisco, California, operates the website at
    <a href="https://mmai.media">mmai.media</a> (the "<strong>Site</strong>"). This Privacy Policy explains what personal
    information we collect through the Site, how we use and protect it, and the choices and rights you have, including
    your rights under the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation (the "<strong>GDPR</strong>") and the California
    Consumer Privacy Act as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (the "<strong>CCPA</strong>").
  </p>

  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p class="legal-callout-title">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The only personal information you give us on the Site is the <strong>email address</strong> you enter in our newsletter
        form, if you choose to subscribe.
      </li>
      <li>
        We use it to send you our newsletter, launch updates, and news about MMAI Media. We do not sell it, rent it, or use it
        for third-party advertising.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You can unsubscribe at any time</strong>, for free, using the link in every email we send, or by emailing us.
      </li>
      <li>
        Our email provider is Brevo, YouTube hosts the videos we embed, and Google reCAPTCHA helps keep bots out of the signup
        form. We do not run our own analytics or advertising trackers on the Site.
      </li>
      <li>
        You have rights to access, correct, and delete your information, and to withdraw consent. See
        <a href="#gdpr-rights">GDPR rights</a> and <a href="#ccpa-rights">California rights</a>, or email
        <a href="mailto:info@mmai.media">info@mmai.media</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
    <p class="legal-toc-title">Contents</p>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#who-we-are">Who We Are</a></li>
      <li><a href="#information-we-collect">Information We Collect</a></li>
      <li><a href="#how-we-use">How and Why We Use Your Information</a></li>
      <li><a href="#newsletter">Newsletter and Unsubscribing</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sharing">Who We Share Information With</a></li>
      <li><a href="#cookies">Cookies, Local Storage, and Similar Technologies</a></li>
      <li><a href="#transfers">International Data Transfers</a></li>
      <li><a href="#retention">How Long We Keep Your Information</a></li>
      <li><a href="#gdpr-rights">Your Rights Under the GDPR (EEA and UK)</a></li>
      <li><a href="#ccpa-rights">Your California Privacy Rights (CCPA)</a></li>
      <li><a href="#children">Children's Privacy</a></li>
      <li><a href="#security">Security</a></li>
      <li><a href="#third-party-links">Third-Party Links</a></li>
      <li><a href="#changes">Changes to This Policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="#contact">Contact Us</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <section id="who-we-are">
    <h2>Who We Are</h2>
    <p>
      MMAI Media LLC, San Francisco, California, United States, is the "controller" of personal data collected through the
      Site under the GDPR and the "business" that collects personal information under the CCPA. You can reach us at
      <a href="mailto:info@mmai.media">info@mmai.media</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="information-we-collect">
    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

    <h3>Information you give us</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Email address.</strong> When you subscribe to our newsletter through the signup form on the Site.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Consent and subscription records.</strong> A record that you ticked the consent box and confirmed your
        subscription, the date and time, and the IP address used. Our email platform may record these so we can demonstrate
        that you consented.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Messages you send us.</strong> If you email us, we receive your email address, any name you include, and the
        content of your message.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Server and technical data.</strong> When you visit the Site, our web server and hosting providers may
        automatically log your IP address, the date and time of the request, the pages and files requested, the referring
        page, and your browser, operating system, and device type.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Data sent to third-party services the Site loads.</strong> To display the Site, the signup form, and embedded
        videos, your browser connects to Google (to load the Inter font from Google Fonts, and to run Google reCAPTCHA on the
        signup form), to YouTube, which Google operates (on pages that embed a YouTube video, to load the video player), and
        to Brevo (to load the signup form's styles and scripts). These providers receive your IP address and standard browser
        information. See <a href="#sharing">Who We Share Information With</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Email engagement data.</strong> Our newsletters are sent through Brevo, which may record whether an email was
        delivered and opened and which links were clicked, along with your email client or device type and approximate
        location inferred from your IP address, using standard techniques such as tracking pixels and redirected links.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
    <p>
      The Site has no user accounts, comments, or checkout. We do not ask for your name, postal address, phone number, or
      payment details, and we do not intentionally collect sensitive personal information (such as health data, government IDs,
      precise location, or information about race, religion, or sexual orientation). We do not currently use our own
      analytics, advertising, or cross-site tracking tools on the Site; the third-party services described in this policy
      operate under their own policies. If that changes, we will update this policy first and, where the law requires, ask
      for your consent.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="how-we-use">
    <h2>How and Why We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>
      We only use personal information for the purposes below. For visitors in the European Economic Area ("<strong>EEA</strong>")
      and the United Kingdom ("<strong>UK</strong>"), the table also shows the legal basis for each purpose under the GDPR.
    </p>

    <div class="legal-table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
            <th scope="col">Information used</th>
            <th scope="col">GDPR legal basis</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>
              Send you a confirmation email, our newsletter, launch updates, and news about MMAI Media, our videos, games, and
              other projects
            </td>
            <td>Email address; subscription records</td>
            <td>Your consent (Art. 6(1)(a))</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              Keep records of your consent, subscription, and unsubscription, and make sure we honor your opt-out
            </td>
            <td>Email address; consent and unsubscribe records</td>
            <td>Legitimate interests in complying with the law and respecting your choices (Art. 6(1)(f))</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Protect the Site and signup form from spam, bots, and abuse; fix technical problems</td>
            <td>IP address; browser and device data; server logs</td>
            <td>Legitimate interests in keeping the Site secure and working (Art. 6(1)(f))</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Respond to your emails and handle privacy requests</td>
            <td>Email address; content of your message</td>
            <td>Legitimate interests in responding to you (Art. 6(1)(f)); legal obligation for privacy requests (Art. 6(1)(c))</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Comply with legal obligations, enforce our <a href={`${base}/terms/`}>Terms of Service</a>, and protect rights and safety</td>
            <td>Any of the above, as needed</td>
            <td>Legal obligation (Art. 6(1)(c)); legitimate interests (Art. 6(1)(f))</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p>
      Providing your email address is voluntary. If you do not provide it, you simply will not receive the newsletter. We do not
      make decisions about you using automated decision-making or profiling that has legal or similarly significant effects,
      and we do not use your information to serve third-party advertising.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where we rely on your consent, you may withdraw it at any time (see
      <a href="#newsletter">Newsletter and Unsubscribing</a>). Withdrawing consent does not affect the lawfulness of
      processing before you withdrew it. Where we rely on legitimate interests, you have the right to object (see
      <a href="#gdpr-rights">Your Rights Under the GDPR</a>).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="newsletter">
    <h2>Newsletter and Unsubscribing</h2>
    <p>
      To subscribe, you enter your email address, tick the box agreeing to receive our newsletters and accepting this Privacy
      Policy, and submit the form. We then send a confirmation email, and we only add you to our mailing list and start
      sending newsletters once you confirm (double opt-in).
    </p>
    <p><strong>You can unsubscribe at any time, free of charge, and without giving a reason.</strong> You can do so by:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        clicking the <strong>unsubscribe link at the bottom of any email we send you</strong>, which takes effect
        automatically; or
      </li>
      <li>
        emailing <a href="mailto:info@mmai.media">info@mmai.media</a> from the address you subscribed with, asking us to
        unsubscribe you. We will process email requests promptly and in any case within 10 business days.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Withdrawing your consent is as easy as giving it. After you unsubscribe, we will stop sending you newsletters and
      marketing emails. We keep only a minimal record of your unsubscription so that we do not email you again (see
      <a href="#retention">How Long We Keep Your Information</a>).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="sharing">
    <h2>Who We Share Information With</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information. We share it only with the following, and only as needed:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Brevo</strong>, our email marketing platform. Brevo stores your email address and subscription records, sends
        our emails, and reports delivery and engagement, acting as our service provider (processor) under its data processing
        terms. Brevo's own handling of data is described in
        <a href="https://www.brevo.com/en/legal/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Brevo's Privacy Policy</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google</strong>, which provides <strong>reCAPTCHA</strong> (spam and abuse protection on the signup form) and
        <strong>Google Fonts</strong> (the Inter typeface). reCAPTCHA collects information such as your IP address, browser and
        device characteristics, and how you interact with the page, to tell humans from bots. This form is protected by
        reCAPTCHA, and the Google
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a> and
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Terms of Service</a> apply.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>YouTube</strong> (operated by Google), which hosts the videos we embed on the Site. When a page with an
        embedded video loads, or when you play the video, YouTube receives your IP address and browser information and may
        set cookies or similar identifiers and collect information about your viewing. This is governed by the
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube Terms of Service</a> and
        the Google Privacy Policy linked above.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Hosting and infrastructure providers</strong> that serve the Site and process technical data such as IP
        addresses and server logs on our behalf.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Authorities and advisers</strong>, where we believe disclosure is required by law, legal process, or a
        government request, or is needed to protect the rights, property, or safety of MMAI Media, our users, or others, and
        to our professional advisers under duties of confidentiality.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A successor</strong>, if MMAI Media is involved in a merger, acquisition, financing, or sale of assets. Your
        information would remain subject to this policy unless you are notified of a change.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not "sell" or "share" personal information as those terms are defined in the CCPA (that is, for money or other
      valuable consideration, or for cross-context behavioral advertising).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="cookies">
    <h2>Cookies, Local Storage, and Similar Technologies</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Our own storage.</strong> The Site does not set cookies of its own. When you use the light/dark theme switch,
        the Site saves your choice (a value named "theme") in your browser's local storage so it can remember it on your next
        visit. This stays on your device and is not sent to us. You can clear it at any time in your browser settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Third-party services.</strong> Google reCAPTCHA, the Brevo signup form, and embedded YouTube videos may set or
        read cookies, local storage, or similar identifiers in your browser to work, to detect abuse, and (for YouTube) to
        record viewing. These are controlled by those providers under their own policies (linked above), and you can block
        them in your browser settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No analytics or advertising trackers of our own.</strong> We do not ourselves use analytics, advertising, or
        social-media tracking cookies or pixels on the Site. (Embedded third-party content such as YouTube videos operates
        under its provider's policies, and our emails may contain a tracking pixel, as described under
        <a href="#information-we-collect">Information We Collect</a>.)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control.</strong> Because we do not track you across other websites and do not
        sell or share your personal information, we do not change how the Site works when your browser sends a Do Not Track
        or Global Privacy Control signal.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can block or delete cookies and local storage through your browser settings, though parts of the signup form may not work if you do.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="transfers">
    <h2>International Data Transfers</h2>
    <p>
      We are based in the United States, and information collected through the Site is transferred to, stored, and processed in
      the United States and in other countries where our service providers operate. If you access the Site from the EEA, the
      UK, or elsewhere outside the United States, your information will be transferred to countries whose data protection laws
      may not offer the same level of protection as the laws where you live.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our service providers may rely on safeguards such as the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses or the
      EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework. By ticking the consent box and subscribing, you explicitly consent to the transfer of
      your email address to the United States after having been informed of these possible risks. You may withdraw your
      consent at any time (see <a href="#newsletter">Newsletter and Unsubscribing</a>).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention">
    <h2>How Long We Keep Your Information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Newsletter email address and subscription records:</strong> until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>After you unsubscribe:</strong> we keep your email address and the date of your unsubscription on a suppression
        list for as long as needed to make sure we do not email you again. You can ask us to erase this record too, and we will
        do so unless we are required or permitted by law to keep it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Emails you send us:</strong> for as long as needed to respond and for a reasonable period afterward in case of
        follow-up, then we delete them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Server logs and technical data:</strong> only as long as needed for security and troubleshooting, in line with
        our hosting providers' log retention practices.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Email engagement data:</strong> held in Brevo for as long as your contact record exists, and deleted when we
        delete that record.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may keep information for longer where the law requires it or where we need it to establish, exercise, or defend legal
      claims.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="gdpr-rights">
    <h2>Your Rights Under the GDPR (EEA and UK)</h2>
    <p>If you are in the EEA or the UK, you have the following rights regarding your personal data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you and receive a copy.</li>
      <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> have inaccurate or incomplete data corrected.</li>
      <li><strong>Erasure:</strong> have your data deleted ("right to be forgotten") in the circumstances the GDPR provides.</li>
      <li><strong>Restriction:</strong> ask us to pause processing of your data in certain circumstances.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Portability:</strong> receive the data you gave us in a structured, commonly used, machine-readable format, and
        have it transmitted to another controller where technically feasible.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Object</strong> to processing based on our legitimate interests. You may also object to direct marketing at
        any time, and we will stop.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time, as described under
        <a href="#newsletter">Newsletter and Unsubscribing</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Complain</strong> to a data protection supervisory authority, for example in the EU country where you live or
        work (a list is on the European Data Protection Board's website, <a href="https://edpb.europa.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">edpb.europa.eu</a>),
        or, in the UK, the Information Commissioner's Office (<a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>).
        We would appreciate the chance to address your concern first.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:info@mmai.media">info@mmai.media</a>. We may need to verify your
      identity (for example, by asking you to confirm from the email address we hold). We respond within one month, which we
      may extend by up to two further months for complex or numerous requests, and we will tell you if we do. There is no fee
      unless a request is manifestly unfounded or excessive.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="ccpa-rights">
    <h2>Your California Privacy Rights (CCPA)</h2>
    <p>
      This section applies to California residents and supplements the rest of this policy. Whether or not MMAI Media currently
      meets the CCPA's applicability thresholds, we extend the rights below to California residents.
    </p>

    <h3>Personal information we collect</h3>
    <p>
      In the past 12 months, we have collected the following categories of personal information, for the purposes described in
      <a href="#how-we-use">How and Why We Use Your Information</a>:
    </p>
    <div class="legal-table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">CCPA category</th>
            <th scope="col">What we collect</th>
            <th scope="col">Source</th>
            <th scope="col">Disclosed for a business purpose to</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Identifiers</td>
            <td>Email address; IP address</td>
            <td>You; your browser or device</td>
            <td>Brevo; hosting providers; Google (reCAPTCHA)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Internet or other electronic network activity</td>
            <td>
              Browser and device type; pages requested; date and time; referring page; email opens and clicks; approximate
              location inferred from IP address
            </td>
            <td>Automatically, from your browser, device, or email client</td>
            <td>Brevo; hosting providers; Google (reCAPTCHA, Google Fonts, YouTube)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      We have not collected any other category of personal information, including commercial or financial information,
      biometric information, professional or education information, audio or visual information, inferences used to build a
      profile about you, or "sensitive personal information" as defined by the CCPA (such as precise geolocation or government
      identifiers). Retention periods are described in <a href="#retention">How Long We Keep Your Information</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>No sale or sharing</h3>
    <p>
      We have not sold or shared (for cross-context behavioral advertising) any personal information in the past 12 months,
      and we do not knowingly sell or share the personal information of anyone under 16. Because we do not sell or share
      personal information, there is nothing to opt out of, and we do not display a "Do Not Sell or Share My Personal
      Information" link. We do not use or disclose sensitive personal information for purposes that would give you a right to
      limit it.
    </p>

    <h3>Your rights</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to know and access:</strong> request the categories and specific pieces of personal information we
        collected about you, the categories of sources, the purposes, and the categories of third parties we disclosed it to.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Right to delete</strong> personal information we collected from you, subject to legal exceptions.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to correct</strong> inaccurate personal information we hold about you.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to opt out</strong> of the sale or sharing of your personal information (we do neither), and
        <strong>to limit</strong> the use of sensitive personal information (we do not collect it).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to non-discrimination:</strong> we will not deny you services, charge you different prices, or give you a
        different quality of service because you exercised your rights.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>How to make a request</h3>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:info@mmai.media?subject=California%20Privacy%20Request">info@mmai.media</a> with the subject line
      "California Privacy Request" and tell us which right you want to exercise. Because we operate only online and have no
      account system, we verify requests by asking you to confirm control of the email address associated with the request. An
      authorized agent may submit a request on your behalf; we may ask for your signed permission and verify your identity
      directly with you.
    </p>
    <p>
      We will confirm receipt within 10 business days and respond within 45 days. If we need more time, we may extend by up to
      45 additional days and will tell you why. Requests are free, and you may make a request to know up to twice in any
      12-month period.
    </p>

    <h3>California "Shine the Light"</h3>
    <p>
      California Civil Code Section 1798.83 lets California residents ask which personal information a business has disclosed
      to third parties for their direct marketing purposes. We do not disclose personal information to third parties for their
      direct marketing purposes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="children">
    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 13.
      If you are under 13, please do not use the signup form or send us personal information. If you believe a child under 13
      has given us their information, email <a href="mailto:info@mmai.media">info@mmai.media</a> and we will delete it.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are in the EEA or the UK and below the age at which you can consent to the processing of your data online in your
      country (between 13 and 16, depending on the country), please ask a parent or guardian to subscribe on your behalf.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="security">
    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational measures designed to protect personal information against
      loss, misuse, and unauthorized access, and we limit access to people and providers who need it. No method of
      transmission over the internet or of electronic storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      If a data breach affects your personal information, we will notify you and the relevant authorities as required by law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="third-party-links">
    <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
    <p>
      The Site links to other platforms, such as YouTube, Spotify, Patreon, Itch.io, Substack, Ko-fi, X, Instagram, Bluesky,
      Twitch, and Medium. Those services have their own privacy practices, which we do not control and are not responsible for.
      Please read their policies before giving them any information.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time, for example when we add features or tools or when the law changes. We will
      post the updated version on this page with a new "Last updated" date. If we make a material change, we will give
      prominent notice on the Site and, where the law requires, notify subscribers by email or ask for your consent again.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>For questions about this policy or to exercise your privacy rights, contact:</p>
    <p>
      MMAI Media LLC<br />
      San Francisco, California, United States<br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:info@mmai.media">info@mmai.media</a>
    </p>
    <p>See also our <a href={`${base}/terms/`}>Terms of Service</a>.</p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
